# evaluator-cog — the names this cog reads. Names only: the values live in
# Doppler (mini-app-polis-ecosystem / dev locally, prd deployed). Run under
# `doppler run -- …`; do not copy this to .env — nothing reads it.
#
# Uncommented names are required in Doppler's dev config, and
# `uv run check-doppler-keys` checks dev holds every one. Commented names
# are optional: the code has a default. In production the Lambda gets these
# from SSM (secrets) and its function environment, both declared in
# mini-app-polis/infra. One section per variable in docs/CONFIGURATION.md.

# API key for Anthropic Claude. Only mode='llm' spends it; the release path
# is deterministic and costs no tokens.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Claude model to use for evaluation. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Base URL for the api-kaianolevine-com instance. Production reads this name;
# every other environment reads KAIANO_API_BASE_URL_DEV, with no fallback
# between them.
KAIANO_API_BASE_URL=https://api.kaianolevine.com

# The same for non-production. Empty is valid and means this process has no
# dev API to talk to.
# KAIANO_API_BASE_URL_DEV=

# This cog's own named API key, matching the machine name it declares to
# KaianoApiClient. There is no fallback — unset or wrong means 401 on every
# call to the API. See ecosystem-standards CD-019.
EVALUATOR_COG_API_KEY=

# Sentry DSN for error tracking.
# SENTRY_DSN_COGS=

# Log level for the fleet's logger. Defaults to INFO. Re-applied at every
# invocation.
# LOGGING_LEVEL=INFO

# GitHub personal access token with read access to mini-app-polis repos.
# Required for the conformance flow to download private repos as zipballs.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Healthchecks.io ping URL for Layer 1 observability. Pinged at the end of a
# fleet pass — which is run_introspection, the once-per-pass job. It is a
# ping and not a check: what it reports is that a pass reached its end.
# HEALTHCHECKS_URL_EVALUATOR=

# Which environment this process is in. Doppler sets it per config
# (development in dev). On Lambda, the infra module sets it to "production".
# ENVIRONMENT=development

# Not here any more, and worth saying why rather than leaving a gap:
#
# AWS_REGION — nothing reads it. The container's boto3 client needed a
# region; the handler creates no client, and Lambda supplies the region
# to anything that does.
#
# EVALUATION_QUEUE_URL — the worker does not read a queue. The Lambda
# event source mapping receives and invokes; the handler is handed a
# message and never asks for one. The API holds the queue URL, because
# the API is what sends.
#
# EVALUATION_QUEUE_CONSUMER_KEY_ID / _SECRET — there is no key. The
# Railway container needed one because a container cannot assume a role;
# the Lambda uses aws_iam_role.worker, which carries exactly the same
# receive-and-delete permissions and expires on its own. The IAM user and
# its key were deleted with the cutover.
#
# PREFECT_API_KEY / PREFECT_API_URL — evaluator-cog does not run under
# Prefect (ADR-0004) and no longer depends on it at all.
